Abstract package-root resolution behind one dual-channel helper so `forge setup`
(and runtime commands) work in BOTH the npm/npx install and a `bun build --compile`
single binary. npm channel is byte-identical; the compiled channel is additive.

- lib/package-root.js: getPackageRoot(diskFallback) — disk-first (npm) → embedded
  extraction (compiled) → loud throw if both fail. FORGE_COMPILED --define is the
  primary compiled signal, Bun.embeddedFiles the fallback. Version-stamped temp dir
  + completion sentinel; post-extract count assertion; exec-bit restore; read+write
  (not copyFileSync — bunfs paths don't support the copyfile syscall).
- scripts/gen-embedded-assets.mjs: generates lib/embedded-assets.generated.mjs
  (gitignored) — per-file Bun import-attribute manifest keyed by true POSIX relpath
  (Bun.embeddedFiles drops directory structure, so a keyed map is required).
- Route asset reads through the helper: setup.js, agents-config.js, config-writer.js,
  team.js (forge team), reset.js (resetHard), bin/forge.js (forge docs).
- .gitattributes LF on embedded trees; build:binary + parity:binary scripts.
- Tests: package-root unit (mode detection, safe-default throw, extraction+exec-bit)
  + embedded-assets-drift completeness/LF gate. Regression: 155 npm-channel tests green.
- Proven in a real compiled binary: 142 assets embed+extract, nested paths intact.

Deferred (filed): Step-1 dynamic-require gap blocks full-binary startup (53770b23);
copyEssentialDocs source-path no-op; full docs/ + plugin-agent embedding → step 3.

Issue: 9460dda1-2e69-4390-8f57-c62462118407

